BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wild About Wildlife\, McCormick's Creek State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260725T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260725T000000
UID:b3229da7049362a6b94456304e5e253e@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:10 am: Springhouse Salamanders- (Hike) Meet Naturalist Kaitlyn
  at Deer Run Shelter to take a short hike on Trail 9 to see what salamande
 rs are living in the Springhouse. We recommend wearing shoes\, you don&rsq
 uo\;t mind getting wet! 11 am-11:30: Predator Protection - (Craft) While m
 ost people know that box turtles use their shells to protect themselves fr
 om predators\, they also have many other unique adaptions. Join the Natura
 list in the Nature Center to meet our Box Turtle ambassador and create a c
 raft to take home. 2 pm-2:45 pm: Live Bird of Prey- (Live Animals) Meet Na
 turalist Jared from Hardy Lake and his bird of prey friends in this intera
 ctive live animal program. Program is being held at the Nature Center Audi
 torium . 3:30 pm-4 pm: Slimy Sallies- (Craft) Why are Salamanders so slimy
 ? Drop by the Nature Center anytime between 3:30-4 pm to learn why slime h
 elps salamanders survive. Meet our live Tiger Salamander and create your o
 wn slime to take home with Naturalist Kaitlyn and Jessica.
LOCATION:McCormick's Creek State Park\, 250 McCormick's Creek Park Road\, 
 Spencer\, IN 47460
URL:on.in.gov/mccormickscreek
X-SOURCE:McCormick's Creek State Park
END:VEVENT
